00:22:55.120 --> 00:22:56.640
Why don't you tell me?

00:22:56.640 --> 00:22:57.940
I'll make sure that they spell it right

00:22:57.940 --> 00:22:59.510
on your grave marker.

00:23:06.430 --> 00:23:09.820
Lift it.

00:23:09.820 --> 00:23:13.230
Do what I say.

00:23:13.230 --> 00:23:24.800
Walk.

00:23:36.620 --> 00:23:37.520
Keep moving.

00:23:37.520 --> 00:23:39.620
Why?

00:23:39.620 --> 00:23:43.690
Soon as we're done, you're just gonna kill me.

00:23:43.690 --> 00:23:44.690
I'll just get it over with.

00:23:44.690 --> 00:23:45.840
I'm tired!

00:23:45.840 --> 00:23:54.380
You're a husband and father.

00:23:54.380 --> 00:23:58.610
Then you owe it to your mate and your children to keep yourself alive for as long as possible, hm?

00:24:00.120 --> 00:24:06.840
- Lift that crate.

00:24:06.840 --> 00:24:21.090
- He went to the Dragoid Katsoth Homeworld?

00:24:21.090 --> 00:24:22.820
- My exact reaction.

00:24:22.820 --> 00:24:24.180
- Why would Tyr walk into the stronghold

00:24:24.180 --> 00:24:25.020
of his mortal enemies?

00:24:25.020 --> 00:24:26.420
- I'll see your question, I'll raise you one.

00:24:26.420 --> 00:24:28.720
What did he do when he got there, look at that.

00:24:28.720 --> 00:24:30.000
Couple of hours after he landed,

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:34.390
That's Tyr, he always loved to party.

00:24:34.390 --> 00:24:43.240
I can't carry it any further.

00:24:43.240 --> 00:24:45.180
Far enough.

00:24:45.180 --> 00:25:00.000
I commend that you don't care.

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:07.200
move until nightfall. I may still be out there in the trees somewhere. And if I see you again,

00:25:07.620 --> 00:25:19.740
I'll kill you. You're keeping me alive. Apparently. Right, aren't you? What if I am?

00:25:20.170 --> 00:25:28.380
I was right about what I was carrying. It was an honor.

00:26:06.010 --> 00:26:08.230
- My lineage was also proud.

00:26:08.230 --> 00:26:09.890
The Kodiak were entrusted with the remains

00:26:09.890 --> 00:26:11.250
of the original progenitor.

00:26:11.250 --> 00:26:13.990
- You've actually seen the body of Drago Museveni?

00:26:13.990 --> 00:26:14.570
- As a child.

00:26:14.570 --> 00:26:16.510
- Drago Kassov came out of nowhere.

00:26:16.510 --> 00:26:20.230
- Mummified remains were enshrined in our fast hood.

00:26:20.230 --> 00:26:21.350
From all over the known worlds

00:26:21.350 --> 00:26:22.790
would make pilgrimages to see it.

00:26:22.790 --> 00:26:24.370
- Maintain focus.

00:26:24.370 --> 00:26:25.870
- We lived under a permanent truce

00:26:25.870 --> 00:26:29.830
and our allies guaranteed our safety.

00:26:30.220 --> 00:26:34.620
until the Drago Katsoth Pride claimed they were the progenitors' rightful keepers.

00:26:34.960 --> 00:26:38.280
Our allies abandoned us. We fought so very fiercely.

00:26:48.130 --> 00:26:53.040
Voice code. Retribution.

00:26:53.960 --> 00:26:55.880
Authorized. Lost is engaged.

00:27:08.540 --> 00:27:13.180
I go almost 70, I presume.

00:27:13.180 --> 00:27:22.500
Spread out to find a Kodiak. Remember, we need him alive, so no mistakes.

00:28:15.930 --> 00:28:19.050
Please, reach for your gun. Give me an excuse.

00:28:19.050 --> 00:28:22.240
You said you'd kill me next time you saw me.

00:28:22.240 --> 00:28:25.310
Care to try your luck?

00:28:25.310 --> 00:28:26.500
I said that I'd kill you.

00:28:26.500 --> 00:28:29.540
I didn't say when.

00:28:49.710 --> 00:28:52.530
the entire Nietzschean battle group and left them chasing their own tails.

00:28:52.530 --> 00:28:54.040
Andromeda kept me up to date.

00:28:54.040 --> 00:28:55.980
It looked like you had everything well in hand.

00:28:55.980 --> 00:28:57.400
Thanks for the vote of confidence.

00:28:57.400 --> 00:28:59.370
You've earned it.

00:28:59.370 --> 00:29:00.000
One thing bothers me.

00:29:00.540 --> 00:29:01.580
What's that?

00:29:01.580 --> 00:29:05.890
I was curious about how you managed to track Tyr, so I had Andromeda review your link-up with the Drift.

00:29:05.890 --> 00:29:09.100
I had no idea you were so good with IS systems.

00:29:09.100 --> 00:29:11.600
Ah, you found my hack!

00:29:11.600 --> 00:29:13.650
I did!

00:29:13.650 --> 00:29:16.270
You rifled through the station's entire database.

00:29:16.270 --> 00:29:18.850
And I found Tyr's departure route.

00:29:18.850 --> 00:29:22.200
Among other things, you copied files from all over the Drift.

00:29:22.200 --> 00:29:26.010
Scientific research reports, archaeological journals, shipping data...

00:29:26.010 --> 00:29:28.910
Somehow I get the feeling that Tyr wasn't all you were looking for.

00:29:28.910 --> 00:29:30.000
Dylan, really?

00:29:30.000 --> 00:29:33.970
think I'm here? I mean you won't let me use Andromeda for running cargo. I'm not

00:29:33.970 --> 00:29:38.130
allowed to mine. God knows you're not paying me. I like your whole idea of the

00:29:38.130 --> 00:29:40.570
Commonwealth but do you really think that's the only thing that's keeping me

00:29:40.570 --> 00:29:47.160
around? I'd prefer to. Come on Dylan. Your entire crew has an ulterior motive.

00:29:47.160 --> 00:29:52.270
Red Ben wants to use your Commonwealth to spread his faith. Harper is in lust

00:29:52.270 --> 00:29:56.300
with your ship. Tyr's always plotting something and God only knows what the

00:29:56.300 --> 00:30:00.000
purple one's up to. Does it really surprise you to find out that I'm no different?

00:30:00.600 --> 00:30:02.490
No, I suppose not.

00:30:02.490 --> 00:30:03.940
I'm here, aren't I?

00:30:03.940 --> 00:30:05.090
For now.

00:30:05.090 --> 00:30:10.600
Okay, the way things are going these days now is all we've got.

00:31:23.360 --> 00:31:26.780
I should leave. Head out on my own.

00:31:26.980 --> 00:31:28.620
And go where? You need a guide.

00:31:31.150 --> 00:31:33.920
Hey, why are you doing this?

00:31:34.560 --> 00:31:36.280
Maybe the madness finally got me, too.

00:32:03.840 --> 00:32:05.770
It's my little kludge.

00:32:05.770 --> 00:32:08.030
See?

00:32:08.030 --> 00:32:10.520
I told him I could find him for you.

00:32:10.520 --> 00:32:11.800
And you.

00:32:11.800 --> 00:32:13.700
Garbage removed, I'd say.

00:32:13.700 --> 00:32:17.020
I'm sorry, Nemo.

00:32:17.020 --> 00:32:19.430
I don't blame you.

00:32:19.430 --> 00:32:22.340
How touching.

00:32:22.340 --> 00:32:24.740
Now, about my reward.

00:32:24.740 --> 00:32:26.150
Of course.

00:32:47.150 --> 00:32:50.100
Intimidation and strength are the only currency an etching needs.

00:32:50.100 --> 00:32:51.370
Don't you agree?

00:32:51.370 --> 00:32:53.370
You kill me and you'll never find your prize.

00:32:53.370 --> 00:32:55.190
That's where intimidation comes in.

00:32:55.190 --> 00:32:57.620
Either you tell us what we want to know,

00:32:57.620 --> 00:32:58.930
or we'll kill your friends.

00:33:04.730 --> 00:33:05.220
Fine.

00:33:05.220 --> 00:33:11.650
Alright.

00:33:11.650 --> 00:33:13.410
It takes care of that.

00:33:13.410 --> 00:33:15.980
Crate.

00:33:15.980 --> 00:33:17.350
I'll lead you to it.

00:33:17.350 --> 00:33:21.920
But you let them go first.

00:33:21.920 --> 00:33:23.010
They come with us.

00:33:23.010 --> 00:33:23.940
For insurance.

00:33:23.940 --> 00:33:25.760
Lead on.

00:33:41.420 --> 00:33:43.390
There's one thing I don't understand.

00:33:43.390 --> 00:33:45.340
Why do you care about these kludges?

00:33:45.340 --> 00:33:47.460
They're nothing.

00:33:47.460 --> 00:33:49.310
- Nothing.

00:33:49.310 --> 00:33:50.880
Who feed you.

00:33:50.880 --> 00:33:52.380
The people who clothe you.

00:33:52.380 --> 00:33:53.220
Weren't for its slave,

00:33:53.220 --> 00:33:56.510
where else the Drago Katzoff pride would cease to exist.

00:33:56.510 --> 00:33:58.090
Ruling over them doesn't make you strong,

00:33:58.090 --> 00:33:59.480
it makes you dependent.

00:34:00.090 --> 00:34:01.400
...and weak.

00:34:01.400 --> 00:34:05.340
Strong enough to turn Kodiak pride to dust.

00:34:05.340 --> 00:34:11.230
Should have killed you.

00:34:11.230 --> 00:34:13.480
It's this way.

00:34:13.480 --> 00:34:16.800
Wait!

00:34:16.800 --> 00:34:19.600
You go first.

00:34:19.600 --> 00:34:21.070
We don't want any surprises.

00:34:21.070 --> 00:34:23.900
Go to hell.

00:34:23.900 --> 00:34:27.940
You see, they do it to themselves.

00:34:31.310 --> 00:34:40.490
It works both ways, doesn't it?

00:34:40.490 --> 00:34:44.080
So long as I'm trying to protect them, you can force me to cooperate.

00:34:44.080 --> 00:34:47.510
But just as soon as they're dead, I'll have nothing to lose.

00:34:47.510 --> 00:34:52.770
Only one problem, there's two of them, and I have a spare.

00:34:52.770 --> 00:34:55.390
Brayon, do as he says.

00:34:55.390 --> 00:34:57.750
You heard her.

00:36:13.820 --> 00:36:14.780
Take it from him.

00:36:30.540 --> 00:36:32.770
You're nothing!

00:36:32.770 --> 00:36:37.240
You're no one!

00:37:18.460 --> 00:37:19.270
I'll be okay.

00:37:36.240 --> 00:37:38.430
- There's no way out.

00:37:38.430 --> 00:37:45.780
Give it up, now.

00:37:45.780 --> 00:37:51.170
- Fine, reseal the cave.

00:37:51.170 --> 00:37:53.030
Pump it full of nerve gas.

00:37:53.030 --> 00:37:54.910
- Excuse us.

00:37:54.910 --> 00:37:56.670
I don't know what kind of game you're playing here,

00:37:56.670 --> 00:37:58.800
but nerve gas, I would have to say is

00:38:00.280 --> 00:38:03.180
As a charge Force Lance pointed at you, they play nice.

00:38:14.280 --> 00:38:15.750
Yes, I believe they are.

00:38:35.470 --> 00:38:37.530
says she's got tomorrow up and running again.

00:38:38.910 --> 00:38:42.110
Pleasant surprise. Rather like

00:38:42.110 --> 00:38:45.270
your arrival. In the old days when

00:38:45.270 --> 00:38:47.360
high guard officers were missing in

00:38:47.360 --> 00:38:49.610
enemy territory, we found them. No matter

00:38:49.610 --> 00:38:51.780
what. These aren't the old days.

00:38:52.360 --> 00:38:53.520
Not yet, but I'm working on it.

00:38:55.230 --> 00:38:57.030
We better get going before they drag our cats off

00:38:57.030 --> 00:39:00.000
bringing more troops. I'll need just

00:39:00.000 --> 00:39:00.700
a few minutes

00:39:00.700 --> 00:39:05.200
Dylan

00:39:05.200 --> 00:39:08.480
thank you

00:39:08.480 --> 00:39:27.120
so

00:39:27.120 --> 00:39:28.960
what will you do

00:39:31.050 --> 00:39:36.390
I had considered staying, though I couldn't quite tell you why.

00:39:38.250 --> 00:39:40.150
You risked your life for whatever is in that crate.

00:39:41.210 --> 00:39:42.970
I'm betting you're not going to just forget about it.

00:39:44.840 --> 00:39:48.580
And even if you wanted to, do you really think the dragons would leave you alone?

00:39:49.620 --> 00:39:52.750
I might ask you the same question.

00:39:54.900 --> 00:39:55.880
Midden is a big planet.

00:39:56.780 --> 00:39:58.020
Brayon and I, we can move.

00:39:58.880 --> 00:39:59.280
Disappear.

00:40:00.540 --> 00:40:03.660
But you could never do that.

00:40:03.660 --> 00:40:08.360
There is another option.

00:40:08.360 --> 00:40:11.680
You and Brayon could come with me.

00:40:11.680 --> 00:40:14.780
Us.

00:40:14.780 --> 00:40:16.020
And join you on your grand adventure?

00:40:16.020 --> 00:40:22.830
I've had enough adventure to last a lifetime.

00:40:22.830 --> 00:40:25.720
All I want is to tend my nets.

00:40:25.720 --> 00:40:27.960
To grow old on the same world where I was born.

00:40:27.960 --> 00:40:29.830
Us.

00:40:31.470 --> 00:40:32.730
On adventures, people die.

00:40:35.090 --> 00:40:37.530
And I don't want to see you or anyone else I care about die.

00:40:38.870 --> 00:40:39.390
Not again.

00:40:40.750 --> 00:40:42.990
I guess that makes me a coward.

00:40:46.120 --> 00:40:47.520
You're much braver than you know.

00:40:52.060 --> 00:40:55.240
So, live well.

00:40:57.580 --> 00:40:58.620
You ain't Gwenen's daughter.

00:41:01.050 --> 00:41:09.140
Live well, Tirana Sassi, out of Victoria, by Barbarossa.

00:41:10.510 --> 00:41:11.010
Hmm.

00:41:34.440 --> 00:41:35.450
Here!

00:41:35.450 --> 00:41:38.100
Are you ever gonna tell me what we're transporting here?

00:41:38.100 --> 00:41:41.940
Something that belongs to me.

00:41:41.940 --> 00:41:47.760
Something that's belonged to me all along.
